11:18: tamber-kind: `12` is a number; a length says its unit (`12px`)
12:21: tamber-kind: `50%`: a length token is px, `rem`, `em` or a named length, not a percentage
13:17: tamber-kind: `calc(1rem + 2px)`: the kernel takes only px inside `calc()`, `min()`, `max()` and `clamp()` until QUEUE's item "`rem`/`em` where the kernel still takes only `px`"
14:25: tamber-kind: a length is one value
15:19: tamber-kind: `10deg`: a length is px, `rem`, `em` or a named length
16:30: tamber-kind: `ink` is a colour, not a length
17:30: tamber-kind: `lift` is a number, not a length
18:29: tamber-kind: `50%`: a number token is a number (`0.5`)
19:23: tamber-kind: `12px` is a length, not a number
20:30: tamber-kind: `space.ok` is a length, not a number
22:11: tamber-kind: `calc(1px + 2)` adds a length and a number
23:13: tamber-kind: `calc(2px * 3px)`: a length times or over a length is no length
25:5: tamber-under-kind: only a colour may vary by an axis `under scheme=dark`: the kernel picks a length's slice without knowing the scheme
26:3: tamber-scheme-fixed: `fixed.length` is a length: `scheme=fixed` marks a colour
27:3: tamber-pair: `paired.length` is a length: `pair=` says what a colour is drawn on
28:3: tamber-kind: `label` overrides a colour role, so it is a colour
30:17: tamber-kind: `rem.token` in `calc(rem.token * 2)`: the kernel takes only px inside `calc()`, `min()`, `max()` and `clamp()` until QUEUE's item "`rem`/`em` where the kernel still takes only `px`"
